<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">companion-part</ansi>

Ends your travels with your companion. They go back to wait in the
Waystone Hollow, taking what they have learned with them, and leave you
the things you gave them or bought for them. They do not come back on
their own: you would have to win them over again.

Nothing your companion says or decides can end the bond by itself, unless
they have come to distrust and dislike you so badly that they will not
stay. Either they ask to part ways and you confirm here, or you use this
command twice within a minute.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Usage ━━━</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">companion-part</ansi>    Part ways (asks once for confirmation).

They do not keep their memories of you. What stays with them is how
they felt about you and one line of how it ended, and that is what they
think of if you come to find them again. If you win them back, you start
afresh. See <ansi fg="command">help companion-hollow</ansi>.
